    "title": "Wisconsin Rapids Man Arrested After Columbia County Highway Chase - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Country Herald Police Reports ,\n7 hours ago Portage, WI – A wanted Wisconsin Rapids man was arrested Tuesday afternoon after allegedly leading deputies on a pursuit in Columbia County, authorities said. According to the Columbia County Sheriff’s Office, deputies received information that 36-year-old Derik Walter was driving in the county despite having an active felony warrant from a 2022 case. Around 1:53 p.m., a sheriff’s sergeant spotted the vehicle on Highway 60 near I-90/94/39. When the sergeant attempted a traffic stop, Walter allegedly threw an item from his vehicle and drove away, exiting onto County Highway CS. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
